{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794262580221301002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"nonfat-wimpy-aurochs","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"4cbae3dbe7b8e56fbace7b55a7144594c2bdc415c80ef8486ab7b4e40b1e4515","event_uuid":"50558e99-6815-436a-af36-e3189f5a5d8b","position":{"commit_sha":"d2af9028142a61d941f0460597c88d94e64a7ff8","position":"1794262554720512001-50558e99-6815-436a-af36-e3189f5a5d8b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"c5c03ab2004c90484caf3129cab177d44dd3363967755fd55dfb8de0b7b99120","event_uuid":"19f5a89d-a33e-4fd5-936b-8ee2be755b11","position":{"commit_sha":"970787beb003c6d60a11a990b5eb9c8432d42d79","position":"1794262580221301001-19f5a89d-a33e-4fd5-936b-8ee2be755b11"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794262554720512001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"19f5a89d-a33e-4fd5-936b-8ee2be755b11","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f86a-c0ce-f107-405f"}],"description":"## Observation\n- `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml` sets `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED: \"1\"` unconditionally on the `Run mutation shard` step of the `bounded mutation gate` job.\n- Run 41939410124 (Gerrit change 3328, 2026-11-04 PST, runner image ubuntu-24.04): every shard log shows `bwrap is installed but cannot create a namespace (bwrap: setting up uid map: Permission denied)` followed by `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED is set: running mutation tests UNSANDBOXED`, and all 7 shards concluded `success`. The only trace of the waiver is a warning line in the step log; `summary.json`, the job conclusion and the Verified vote are identical to a sandboxed pass.\n- Run 42702801672 (change 3335, 2026-11-09 PST, ubuntu-26.04): bwrap 0.11.1 starts, the waiver line is absent, and the sandboxed path ran.\n\n## Impact\nOn any runner where bwrap cannot create a namespace, mutated code runs with write access to the whole runner and the gate still reports green as though it were sandboxed. The 2026-08-26 destructive-mutation incident (`e668-b496-e264-4283`) is the hazard the sandbox exists for. The waiver also hid the basetemp bind-mount defect (`unwasteful-increased-colt`) for its whole life, because the sandboxed path never executed in CI.\n\n## Approach\nRemove the unconditional waiver from the mutation lane so the gate fails closed (`SandboxUnavailable`) when bwrap cannot start, now that the hosted image starts bwrap. Update the workflow comments that say hosted Ubuntu denies namespaces. Make the sandbox mechanism (or the waiver) visible in `summary.json` so a reader of the evidence can tell a sandboxed pass from a waived one. No new config key, env var or feature flag.\n\n## Scope\n- `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml` (drop the waiver, fix the stale comments)\n- `scripts/mutation_gate.py` (record the mechanism in the summary; turn `SandboxUnavailable` into a `GateError` so the failure lands in `summary.json`)\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py`, `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` fixtures if they pin the env block\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The mutation lane no longer sets `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED`, and a shard on a runner without a working sandbox fails with a summary that names the missing sandbox.\n- [ ] `summary.json` records which sandbox mechanism ran each shard.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"248a-9e8d-afc3-4518","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Mutation lane waives the sandbox unconditionally, so a runner where bwrap cannot start reports green as if sandboxed","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["50558e99-6815-436a-af36-e3189f5a5d8b","19f5a89d-a33e-4fd5-936b-8ee2be755b11"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794262580221301002,"uuid":"d087db98-aeac-4eb1-b73f-1c1332f3ac55"}